WEBVTT

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:08.890
I'm sorry.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:11.100
This is the best I can do right now.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.030
Why did it have to come to this?

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:24.420
So you feed on the information particles known as runes?

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.680
Humans have lots of runes!

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.550
Memories! Past! Life!

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:33.680
So once you've consumed all the memories, you move on to the information called "life"?

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.640
Eating all of this...

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.970
Why did Marie have to die for you?!

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:43.100
I didn't kill her! The Valvrave did!

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.600
There's no difference!

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.300
Go blame the humans who locked me in

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.110
just so they could use the runes.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.120
What—

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.160
So the JIORian scientists turned you into an engine?

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.490
Through you, the Valvrave collects and uses runes.

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:01.060
Yeah! It's not my fault!

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.500
I do eat a little, too, though.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:06.890
I think she's telling the truth.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:07.830
Teacher?

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.040
I examined Marie's body.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.550
The amount of kynurenic acid in her brain and the red blood cells in her blood is abnormally low.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.340
Far too low for someone who had been healthy up until then.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.720
This supports the theory that her runes had been eaten.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:23.540
Tokishima.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:27.640
While slight, the same symptoms showed up on your physical.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:28.860
What?

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:34.250
If you keep on piloting the Valvrave, you will end up just like Marie.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.490
An empty shell.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.870
Huh? Where—

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:37.220
Hey, who are you?

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.740
I'm—

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.790
Hey, who are you?

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.740
I—

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.490
You there!

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.960
Who—

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:48.870
Haruto!

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:51.840
Haruto?

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:56.290
That's right! I'm Haruto!

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.050
Do you know me?

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:02.340
Haruto... Haruto...

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.720
Who's Haruto?

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:06.140
Wait—

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.150
No! Stay away!

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:18.620
Who am I?

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.490
What are you?!

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.390
Tokishima!

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:37.030
Tokishima, we've got a red alert!

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:38.500
You have to sortie with the Valvrave!

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.340
The Valvrave...

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.380
Unit 5 goes first! Got that, Haruto?

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.200
Hey, Haruto!

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:11.200
Haruto, what are you doing?

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.500
Sorry!

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:14.410
Are you okay? Can you stand?

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.210
Yeah, I'm fine!

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.750
Stand aside! I'm going first!

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:19.840
No need for that.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:21.880
But the enemy's at the gates!

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.210
Not at all.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.720
I sounded a fake alarm.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:30.220
I needed to test whether our weapons function properly before making a move.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:33.980
He was testing me...

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:38.850
We will ally with the Dorssian royalists for the time being.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:40.710
The royalists?

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:44.490
They wish to return to the aristocratic state from before the coup.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.240
Bluntly put, they are an anti-government organization.

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:50.490
They offered to provide us with supplies.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:53.240
Why would they help us?

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.050
It's simple.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:57.830
They need our help as well.

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:02.280
This is a Dorssian submarine, "The Phantom".

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:06.760
The royalists want us to destroy it in exchange for supplies.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.760
I see. Give and take, huh?

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:12.870
The operation will commence in 32 hours.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.520
I'll brief everyone on their mission one hour from now.

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:17.180
An operation...

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.020
Wait!

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:21.140
Shouldn't we look for Rukino first?

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:23.610
She's still MIA!

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:30.110
Remember this:

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:34.120
the most important thing for a soldier is to come home alive.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.040
That wound...

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.400
Just a scratch.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:41.040
It's a small price to pay for your life.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:44.550
<i>He saved my life during the collapse?</i>

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.060
Hey, guys.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:58.560
You showed up early.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.310
I do that every now and then.

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:03.970
It seems they found A-Drei.

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:07.080
So I heard. His injuries aren't too severe, apparently.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.450
Good to hear.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:11.000
That guy's got the devil's own luck.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:14.680
For former royalty, he's got a knack for survival.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:15.950
Survival, huh?

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.660
Not a concept you're too familiar with, huh?

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.470
Says the one who forced me to survive.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.110
Did you forget what happened 12 years ago?

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:28.340
Ah, that.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.700
It was the first time I ever feared for my life.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.920
Man, that was a disaster.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:38.150
We're told to wipe out a terrorist organization, and what do you bring to the fight?

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:39.600
A couple handguns.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.910
<i>You're</i> the one who ran off improperly equipped!

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:46.520
I was planning on preparing meticulously!

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.240
Oh, is that how it went?

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:51.460
You kept going on about not going by the book.

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:54.580
You were a bookworm then, and you're a bookworm now.

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:56.740
I knew you'd take way too long with your "preparation".

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:59.890
You're always quick to forget whenever it benefits you.

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:01.120
Sure, whatever.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.340
We almost died back there.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:05.710
We were lucky as hell.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:09.630
No. We were saved by Colonel Cain.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:15.640
I can still remember the words he said to us back then.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:18.180
What an amazing man.

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:20.890
I see.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:26.060
Write me off this afternoon's meeting. Give me a report on it.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.380
Got something better to do?

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:30.380
The colonel wants to see me.

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:32.740
I'm to go to a villa in Grünau.

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:34.240
Grünau?

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:35.490
Is something the matter?

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:39.240
Never mind. Watch your back.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:41.870
What am I, a kid?

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.100
Grünau...

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:52.040
<i>I have to fight.</i>

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:55.080
<i>For Shoko and everyone else.</i>

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:58.210
<i>We need to find Rukino, too.</i>

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.270
I have to.

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:04.890
Watch out. You're the same.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:06.360
The same how?

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:07.850
You have less runes.

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:09.320
Did Haruto hijack you?

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:13.290
I eat... You'll end up losing your memories and your life, too.

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:14.500
I don't care.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:16.750
Now, answer my question.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:20.440
Can only modified JIORians pilot Valvraves?

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:21.710
Modified?

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:23.790
Like the students of Sakimori Academy.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.590
Maybe.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:28.290
The others were no good at all.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:29.790
Disgusting.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:31.710
You wouldn't do either.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:34.050
You look like you taste bad.

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:40.620
Some call it the Castle of No Return.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:44.240
The colonel spends his off-duty time there regularly.

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:47.130
It's in Grünau if I remember correctly.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.010
I knew it.

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:51.360
I'm glad I heard you out.

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:54.360
There are lots of bizarre rumors about the villa.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:59.900
It got its name because people who are taken there are never seen again.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:01.980
Sounds lovely.

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:05.120
I'd dig into it right away, but my other duties take priority.

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:08.790
Hey, can you give me its location?

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.450
We have plans in motion. Don't do anything stupid.

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:13.440
Relax, it's not like that.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:18.590
I just want to carve some keywords into my memory, since I smell some juicy intel behind this.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.170
Are you sure about this?

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:31.290
Can we really bench two more pilots?

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:34.070
You two are our best bet for finding Rukino Saki.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:38.990
Your CQC is the next best after mine, and your hacking will prove useful for this operation.

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.770
All right, I'll bite.

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:45.830
Not to mention you're the only one besides me who knows how Rukino Saki's current body looks.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:47.850
Akira, remember!

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:49.990
Don't drink the water! And do you have your phone?

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:51.000
I do.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.410
Shouldn't I stay?

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:55.980
You and I have our own tasks.

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:59.880
Otamaya! Prep the Valvraves so they can take off at any moment!

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:22.030
The Phantom, a ship whose purpose is unknown and which doesn't exist according to Dorssian army records.

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:25.320
The royalists don't have the equipment to track an underwater target.

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:27.790
Is that why they need us?

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:31.640
It's easy to trace once we figured out which waterway it's using.

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:34.290
The people in charge of it let their guard down.

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.160
What's that emblem?

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:37.750
I've never seen it before.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.920
It doesn't belong to the army or the nobility.

00:11:58.120 --> 00:11:59.440
Now,

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:02.930
it's time you revealed your true colors, Cain.

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:09.450
Stolen transport located! All soldiers, assemble immediately!

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:10.950
I repeat:

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:15.460
stolen transport located! All soldiers, assemble immediately!

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:17.710
How convenient.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:20.210
This'll thin the castle security.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:23.450
I'll be using you to my advantage, dear students.

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:43.450
We'll need the impact boosters again further on.

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.700
The same insignia again?

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:59.880
<i>X, I know that you respect Colonel Cain.</i>

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:05.080
<i>I also know that you have no intention of listening to me.</i>

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:08.390
<i>But even so, I want to tell you this.</i>

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:10.820
<i>I saw things.</i>

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:16.260
<i>I saw him do things that no ordinary person could do.</i>

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:18.770
<i>I know for certain that he's not human.</i>

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:20.150
H-Neun.

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:23.780
You really do have the nose of a bloodhound.

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:30.160
But if this mission is so important, you shouldn't have tried to carry it out alone.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.930
I was invited here.

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:35.410
I'm just a little early.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:41.170
I see. Quite a change from your habitual tardiness.

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:44.170
Did you come alone?

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:52.150
You always need a friend to watch your back.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:56.320
That's quite unlike you to say so.

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:03.110
I remember the words you said when you saved us twelve years ago.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:14.950
Are you all right?

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:16.960
Yes...

00:14:17.270 --> 00:14:19.640
Never ask a friend to watch your back.

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:22.960
Have the strength to protect both your friend and your back!

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.230
Yes, sir!

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:28.940
Today, you say the exact opposite.

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:31.220
X would cry if he could hear you.

00:14:35.030 --> 00:14:39.230
I see, so he said that?

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:40.600
"He"?

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:48.690
Ah, I damaged my collection.

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:54.490
I've identified the bridge, the engine room, and the reserve battery room.

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:57.750
However, this hatch isn't present on the ship's schematics.

00:14:58.130 --> 00:14:59.210
What's behind it?

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:00.250
We're about to find out.

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:23.270
Führer?

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:24.980
What are you doing here?

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:28.490
Which unit do you belong to? Have you met with Cain?

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:32.490
What? My uniform is obviously from Karlstein!

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.330
Karlstein?

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:35.980
What are you doing here?

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:37.490
What obligates me to answer you?

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:44.000
Has the ceremony still not begun?

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.340
It speaks?

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.460
Is he part of the entertainment, Cain?

00:15:47.810 --> 00:15:50.840
No. Sorry for the disturbance.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:56.220
I hope you understand. We have quite an important ceremony going on today.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:02.730
What's this?

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:10.570
It's the same light as the Valvraves' and Pino's.

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.740
Are they harvesting runes?

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:17.440
So runes weren't a JIORian discovery?

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:19.580
Dorssians use runes, too.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:20.460
But why?

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:27.720
The huge amount of runes needed for the ceremony wasn't easy to acquire.

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:30.940
The ship served us well.

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:33.880
Another shipment will arrive today.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:38.090
Cain, I sure hope he's not the one.

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:41.020
I demanded a young intellectual.

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:43.850
Yes, I did not forget.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:48.900
The young body I prepared for you will arrive shortly.

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:50.570
No way!

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:52.990
Rejoice, H-Neun.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:57.570
X-Eins's body will soon belong to my comrade.

00:16:57.880 --> 00:16:59.530
You bastard!

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:03.290
We should sound the gun salute.

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:19.960
Are you satisfied? You just averted your eyes from reality.

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:21.640
What do you mean?

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:26.410
This doesn't change the fact that the Dorssians are collecting runes for some reason.

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:30.190
Even if we destroyed this ship, a second and a third Phantom will take its place.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:33.530
You're saying there'd be just more sacrifices?

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:38.780
You can run away all you want, but the world won't stop moving.

00:17:39.170 --> 00:17:42.040
So what should I do then?

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:47.040
These tremors... Artillery?

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:53.760
I thought this spot was safe!

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:54.880
Calm down!

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:59.200
Open the right rear hatch!

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:00.430
Unit 5, launch!

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:07.700
I'll tank the heavy fire!

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:09.400
Satomi, cover me!

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.590
Can't you shoot them down?

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:15.520
As if I could!

00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:16.630
I must go back!

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:18.030
I need to pilot Unit 1 and—

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:19.530
There's no need for that.

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:22.090
Renbokoji Satomi, can you hear me?

00:18:22.090 --> 00:18:24.410
L-Elf? Yes, I hear you.

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:26.070
Tokishima Haruto's injured.

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:27.560
You pilot Unit 1.

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:28.260
What?

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:29.500
Tokishima's hurt?

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:33.650
What's wrong? Are you going to sit there trembling, waiting for your dear sister's return?

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:37.220
Hey! L-Elf! L-Elf!

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:38.580
Don't interfere.

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:39.720
What are you even doing?

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:44.310
All the students of your academy ought to be able to pilot a Valvrave.

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:47.470
That's not the point! Piloting that unit means—

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:51.560
He won't die right away. You're still alive, aren't you?

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:53.750
We have enough people.

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:57.070
If the students take turns in piloting Unit 1,

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:01.570
at least we won't have to worry about the pilots running out of rune.

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:04.210
An immortal army.

00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:05.700
Are you fucking kidding me?!

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:07.960
You knew all along!

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.790
That's why you made sure Yamada and me didn't get on the transport!

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.340
Don't misunderstand.

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:13.960
You're not apt for combat anymore.

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:15.090
What?

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:19.380
We can't afford to let a coward who can't even fight properly pilot Unit 1.

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:28.870
You... You don't understand!

00:19:30.050 --> 00:19:33.400
You've no idea how it feels to have your memories and life sucked out of you!

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:38.030
Then do you understand how it feels for me to be completely powerless?

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:42.280
If only I could pilot a Valvrave...

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:53.210
I'm gonna overheat!

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:02.900
You were right.

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:07.560
Looking the other way won't change the world.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:11.730
So I'll—

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:18.490
Damn, I can't keep this up!

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:25.740
He's running away?!

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:27.740
Where are you going, Haruto?

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:29.240
It's the right move.

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:34.000
50 left. 40. 30. 20.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.420
Go!

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:46.110
The harakiri blade softened the bedrock in the area.

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:50.220
Add an active volcano, the temperature of the underground waters,

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:51.970
and the shock to the ground.

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:54.140
The conclusion is clear.

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:20.260
I won't let anyone take it!

00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:21.690
I won't share it with anyone!

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:23.790
This curse is mine to bear!

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:25.230
Prepare yourself, then.

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:28.090
I'll use you until you're worn out!

00:21:28.090 --> 00:21:29.850
I don't care!

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:31.950
Before my body collapses,

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:32.770
I'll...

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:41.980
...put an end...

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:43.110
...to this war!

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:03.130
Colonel!

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:04.350
Are you all right?

00:22:04.350 --> 00:22:06.100
The eruption—

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:12.510
What happened here?

00:22:14.610 --> 00:22:17.440
That's H-Neun's.

00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:20.940
I feel bad for him, X-Eins.

00:22:22.850 --> 00:22:25.180
Um, what exactly—

00:22:27.890 --> 00:22:30.070
We have to start the ceremony over from scratch.

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:38.420
We'll need a new food source.

00:24:12.430 --> 00:24:15.890
PREVIEW

00:24:14.280 --> 00:24:18.490
Next time, episode 18: A Father's Wish.

00:24:19.270 --> 00:24:24.390
Valvrave the Liberator... The system that unveils the world.

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:27.440
EPISODE 18

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:27.440
A Father's Wish
